Now I understand the code. The task: refactor to eliminate duplicated logic between `parseRegistryRecord` and `parseManifestRecord`, and between `parseRegistryQuantity` and `parseManifestQuantity`, while preserving the behavioral differences:

Registry record parsing (`parseRegistryRecord`):
- text fields: decoded verbatim, no trimming, no blank check (blank checked later by `validate` with different message)
- error type: `*FormatError` with Position, Batch, Field, Reason
- error reasons: "required field is missing", "must be a JSON string", "must be valid UTF-8 text: malformed bytes or lone surrogate escapes are rejected instead of being replaced with U+FFFD"
- duplicate check first: "field appears more than once; duplicate fields are not allowed" (duplicate checked BEFORE unknown fields)
- unknown: "unknown field; only \"batch\", \"product\", \"quantity\" and \"unit\" are allowed"
- quantity: `parseRegistryQuantity` — errors: "must be a JSON integer between 1 and %d", "must be an integer no greater than %d", "must be greater than zero". Note: registry quantity rejects negatives via `token[0] == '-'` check with isJSONInteger; allows leading zeros? isJSONInteger allows "007"? Yes — registry accepts leading zeros (token from validated JSON can't have leading zeros anyway since JSON spec forbids... actually encoding/json would reject `007` as invalid JSON at the decoder level. But the RawMessage comes from `json.Unmarshal(batchesRaw, &elems)` which validates. So leading zeros can't appear. Fine.)
- field order of checks: duplicate → unknown → batch → product → unit → quantity (missing check for quantity comes after text fields)

Manifest record parsing (`parseManifestRecord`):
- text fields: trimmed via NormalizeField, must be non-blank
- error type: plain errors wrapped by caller into `*ManifestRecordError`
- error reasons: `record has unknown field %q; only batch, product, quantity and unit are allowed`, `record lists field %q more than once`, `missing required field %q`, `field %q must be a JSON string`, `*EncodingError{Field: name}`, `field %q must not be blank: %w`
- Order: unknown/duplicate checked together in one loop (unknown first per field, then duplicate) — note order differs from registry! In manifest, iteration over members in source order: for each field, if unknown → error; if dup → error. So for a record with an unknown field appearing before a duplicate, manifest reports unknown; registry reports duplicate first (since it checks duplicates across all fields first). Must preserve this difference!
- quantity: `parseManifestQuantity` — errors: `field "quantity" must be a JSON integer between 1 and %d`, `field "quantity" must be a JSON integer without sign, fraction or exponent`, `field "quantity" must be a JSON integer without leading zeros`, `field "quantity" must be an integer no greater than %d`, `field "quantity" must be greater than zero`. Manifest rejects leading zeros explicitly; registry's isJSONInteger-based check would accept them (but can't occur in valid JSON).

Also the batch-id attachment logic is duplicated (countField==1, findField, unmarshalStringStrict; manifest additionally NormalizeField).

And `validateManifestInput` vs `Register`'s inline checks vs `validateForSave` — those are also somewhat duplicated but the task focuses on "对单条批次记录的字段检查、文本解码和数量判断" between the two sources (batch-register reading registry file and batch-import manifest). The task says: "这两处对单条批次记录的字段检查、文本解码和数量判断存在重复逻辑" — the two places being 登记文件读取 (decode/parseRegistryRecord) and 到货清单导入 (parseManifestRecord). So the refactor target is parseRegistryRecord/parseManifestRecord and parseRegistryQuantity/parseManifestQuantity.

Plan:
